{
  "name": "tower",
  "doc": "A tower of masonry on a round platform: a lighthouse (a round body with pilasters that flare at the foot, bands, a cove under the gallery, the gallery and its rail, the drum, the lantern with its panes and its lens, the dome, a lightning rod). A house next to it is a model of its own. The option hollow gives the wall and a spiral stair inside at the near level. The ledge, the bands and the flare are over the platform, the other heights over the ground. Each size can have its source; a size with no source is an estimate, and the receipt says so. The origin is on the ground at the center of the platform. The people build it as on a site: a mason lays the platform and the body, a smith makes the lantern, a mason makes the stair, and a surveyor marks the site.",
  "sources": [
    "The sources of each size come with the order; the receipt lists them."
  ],
